messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-i386.c
Line: 626
Function: coff_i386_rtype_to_howto
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: When handling R_SECREL32 with no defined hash entry, the code walks the section list using sym->n_scnum to select asection *s, but does not verify that sym->n_scnum is within the number of sections. If sym->n_scnum exceeds the section count (malformed input), s becomes NULL and s->output_section is dereferenced, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

Source context:
